  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The mean and variance of a set of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;numbers are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn></math> respectively. The mean and variance of another set of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> numbers are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;respectively. If the variance of all the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math> numbers in the two sets is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p>"
  },
